# P02 scope

**Provisional title:** Exact Query Obstructions in Characteristic-Two Modal Computation.

**Central question:** Which exact oracle tasks are excluded by linear modal distinguishability in characteristic two, and why does genuine phase kickback fail to restore the familiar character-transform mechanism?

**Thesis:** Under complete injective linear readout and a fixed pointwise oracle, direct-sum discrimination and secret-polynomial span bounds imply Deutsch one-query impossibility, DJ one-query impossibility, and BV q>=n. Standard XOR gives matching upper bounds 2 andn for Deutsch and BV. Nilpotent-ring kickback exists without a nonsingular Fourier analyzer.

## Principal clusters

ALG-002 exact Deutsch; ALG-003 DJ one-query obstruction with 2 <=Q<=2^(n-1)+1 under QXOR; ALG-004 exact BV=n under QXOR; ALG-005 kickback/Fourier separation, supported by006/007. ALG-001 is an antecedented/elementary discrimination ingredient, not a standalone novel theorem. ALG-011 is standard reversible oracle embedding. ALG-010 reproduces known UNIQUE-SAT as a positive control. ALG-012 distinguishes classical full-description readout.

## Nonnegotiable access assumptions

No cost-free inspection of the full state vector, symbolic coefficients or support. Exactness means every possible outcome has the correct label. Collected complete linear instruments must be injective; discarded or postselected branches cannot be silently ignored. Ancillas may be arbitrary but gates and preparations are independent of the secret. Readout/adaptive branches use the explicitly proved recorded direct-sum construction.

Lower bounds allow arbitrary fixed invertible G0,G1 in the pointwise interface; matching upper bounds require an informative oracle such as QXOR. G0=G1 makes the entire family identical, so the broad upper-bound wording must never reappear. Ring kickback lives in a separately declared enriched/shared scalar contract and does not by itself provide an operational query advantage.

## Exclusions and article shape

No general optimal DJ count above the one-query obstruction; no arbitrary-size Simon no-go; no all-search theorem from failed conventional Grover diffusion; no unique discovery of the polynomial method, MQT, finite-field computation or UNIQUE-SAT. Full chain-ring contextuality/protocol theory belongs to P01. Current finite Simon evidence is a supplement diagnostic, not a P02 primary theorem.

A focused article or note is justified only if the exact-contract lower bounds or the combined separation remain substantive after priority review. If they are already explicit in prior literature, change format or retain as a supplement rather than manufacture a new paper.
